Dear Sir/Madam,

Re: Death of {testatorName} — Account Holder

I am writing to notify you of the death of {testatorName}, who passed away on {dateOfDeath} (death certificate number: {deathCertificateNumber}).

I am the {executorRole} of the estate and enclose a certified copy of the death certificate. Please freeze all accounts held solely or jointly in the name of the deceased pending production of the grant of {grantType}.

I should be grateful if you would confirm in writing:

1. The account number(s) and sort code(s) of all accounts held by the deceased;
2. The balance of each account as at the date of death;
3. Any outstanding loans, overdrafts, or other liabilities as at the date of death;
4. Whether any direct debits or standing orders are in place that should be cancelled.

Please direct all further correspondence to the address below.

Yours faithfully,

{executorName}
{executorAddress}

Dear Sir/Madam,

Re: Life Insurance Policy No. {policyNumber} — Claim on Death of {testatorName}

I am writing to make a claim under the above policy following the death of the life assured, {testatorName}, who passed away on {dateOfDeath}.

Details of the deceased:
- Full name: {testatorName}
- Date of birth: {testatorDateOfBirth}
- Date of death: {dateOfDeath}
- Death certificate number: {deathCertificateNumber}

I enclose the following documents in support of this claim:

1. Original or certified copy of the death certificate;
2. The original policy document (or a declaration of loss if unavailable);
3. Completed claim form (if required by your institution);
4. Proof of identity of the claimant.

The benefit is claimed by {beneficiaryName} as {beneficiaryRelationship} to the deceased. Please confirm receipt of this claim and advise of any further documentation required.

Please contact me at the address below with any queries.

Yours faithfully,

{claimantName}
{claimantAddress}

Dear Sir/Madam,

Re: Pension Scheme: {schemeName} — Membership No. {membershipNumber} — Death of Member {testatorName}

I am writing to notify you of the death of {testatorName} (date of birth: {testatorDateOfBirth}; scheme membership number: {membershipNumber}), who passed away on {dateOfDeath} (death certificate number: {deathCertificateNumber}).

I am the {executorRole} of the estate and am writing to request the following information:

1. The current value of the pension pot or any lump sum death benefit payable;
2. Whether a valid expression of wishes / nomination of beneficiaries is on file;
3. The trustee's process for determining the distribution of any death benefit;
4. Whether any dependant's pension is payable and, if so, to whom;
5. Whether any annuity is in payment and whether it contains a guarantee period with amounts outstanding.

I enclose a certified copy of the death certificate and shall provide a copy of the grant of {grantType} once it has been issued.

Please contact me at the address below with any queries.

Yours faithfully,

{executorName}
{executorAddress}

Dear Sir/Madam,

Re: Application to Transfer Title — {propertyAddress} (Title Number: {titleNumber})

I am writing to apply for the transfer of registered title in respect of the above property following the death of the registered proprietor, {testatorName}, on {dateOfDeath}.

I am the {executorRole} of the estate, acting under a grant of {grantType} issued by {grantingCourt} on {grantDate} (grant reference: {grantReference}).

The property is to be transferred to {beneficiaryName} of {beneficiaryAddress} in accordance with the terms of the {dispositionType}.

I enclose the following documents:

1. Completed application form (AP1 or equivalent);
2. Original or office copy of the grant of representation;
3. Certified copy of the death certificate;
4. Completed transfer deed (TR1 or equivalent) signed by the executor(s);
5. Evidence of payment of any applicable stamp duty or land transaction tax;
6. Identity verification documents for the transferee.

Please acknowledge receipt and confirm the expected registration timescale.

Yours faithfully,

{executorName}
{executorAddress}

Dear Sir/Madam,

Re: Transfer of Vehicle Registration — {vehicleRegistrationNumber} ({vehicleYear} {vehicleMake} {vehicleModel})

I am writing to apply for the transfer of the above vehicle's registration following the death of the registered keeper, {testatorName}, on {dateOfDeath} (death certificate number: {deathCertificateNumber}).

I am the {executorRole} of the estate. The vehicle is to be transferred to {beneficiaryName} of {beneficiaryAddress}.

I enclose the following documents:

1. Certified copy of the death certificate;
2. The vehicle registration document (logbook / certificate of title) or a declaration of loss if unavailable;
3. Completed transfer application form;
4. Evidence of my authority as {executorRole} (copy of grant of {grantType} or letters of administration);
5. Identity documentation for the new keeper.

Please advise whether any further steps are required to update the insurance records or to cancel any road tax / registration label.

Yours faithfully,

{executorName}
{executorAddress}

Dear Sir/Madam,

Re: Death of Taxpayer — {testatorName} — Tax Reference: {taxReference}

I am writing to notify you of the death of {testatorName} (date of birth: {testatorDateOfBirth}; tax reference: {taxReference}), who passed away on {dateOfDeath} (death certificate number: {deathCertificateNumber}).

I am the {executorRole} of the estate, appointed under a grant of {grantType} issued on {grantDate} (grant reference: {grantReference}).

I am writing to:

1. Register the death with your authority and close the deceased's personal tax account;
2. Obtain details of any outstanding tax liabilities or refunds owed for the period up to and including the date of death;
3. Enquire as to any {incomeType} returns required for the final tax year;
4. Obtain guidance on any estate or inheritance tax obligations arising from the death.

Please confirm receipt of this notification and advise of any forms required. I enclose a certified copy of the death certificate and a copy of the grant of representation.

Yours faithfully,

{executorName}
{executorAddress}
